---
/* Home, "Who's behind it": the last thing before the closing. A small version of About's portrait
   card that you can pick up (PortraitCard, from the drawer), the same crew list About uses with my
   name against every role (CrewList), one line in About's own words, and a real link to /about/.
   Every word is About's already: the line is its lede and meta description, the roles are its
   crew list, the caption is its portrait's.

   It sits after the client marks and before the closing, well below the first screen, so the lazy
   portrait never touches the first paint. It is a neutral section, so it also keeps the quote band
   and the closing apart. Styles: the "Who's behind it" block in src/styles/pages/home.css. */
import CrewList from '../ephemera/CrewList.astro';
import PortraitCard from '../ephemera/PortraitCard.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';

const first = site.ownerName.split(' ')[0];
const crew = ['Strategy', 'Design', 'The build', 'Photos, when needed'];
---

<section class="bh" aria-labelledby="bh-h">
  <div class="bh-in">
    <PortraitCard sizes="(max-width: 40rem) 11rem, 14rem" />
    <div class="bh-say">
      <p class="label">Who's behind it</p>
      <h2 id="bh-h">
        One person, <b>start to finish.</b>
      </h2>
      <p class="bh-line">
        I'm {first}. I plan, design and build every site myself, so the person you meet on day one
        is the same person who hands you the finished site.
      </p>
      <div class="bh-crew">
        <CrewList roles={crew} />
      </div>
      <a class="bh-more" href="/about/">
        More about me
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
